  "sources": {
    "katigate_home": "https://katigate.com/en/sahit - merged upcoming saait table: BS date, AD date, weekday, tithi label per ceremony-day row; the ceremony column does not survive text extraction (attributions come from the per-ceremony pages).",
    "katigate_pages": "https://katigate.com/en/sahit/{vivah,bratabandha,griha-pravesh,griha-aramba,pasni,vyaparik} - per-month concatenated digit-string day lists for BS 2083 (upcoming months only; passed months of the BS year are not re-listed), next-3 event chips (month anchors), page-title full-year claimed counts, closure FAQ copy.",
    "honesty_note": "katigate.com/en/sahit states the dates follow the sahit list published each year from the traditional panchang tables, used by priests across Nepal; if the official list for a year is not published yet the page may show estimated dates calculated from the classical rules, to be checked against the published list once it is out. The published/estimated honesty tier is stated by the publisher.",
    "dekhopanchang_ssy": "https://dekhopanchang.com/en/learn/sarvartha-siddhi-yoga - the complete Sarvartha Siddhi vara-nakshatra table (classical: Muhurta Chintamani, Nirnaya Sindhu), weekday x Moon nakshatra at sunrise; yoga runs sunrise -> end of the qualifying nakshatra; documented overrides: Rahu Kaal suspension, Bhadra (Vishti) karana, Panchak reduction, eclipse.",
    "hinducalendar_amrit": "https://hinducalendar.app/muhurat/amrit-siddhi/2026 - Amrit Siddhi = exactly one nakshatra per weekday (Sun-Hasta, Mon-Mrigashira, Tue-Ashwini, Wed-Anuradha, Thu-Pushya, Fri-Revati, Sat-Rohini); dated 2026 instance windows, IST computed for Ujjain; windows can start mid-run when the nakshatra begins after sunrise - a convention collision with the at-sunrise convention, recorded not applied."
  },
